1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
At 10:22 in the morning on June 4th, 1942,

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,600
American dive bombers fell out of the clouds above the Japanese carrier Kaga.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,000
Within six minutes, three of the carriers that had attacked Pearl Harbor were burning.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
For decades, this was told as five minutes of bad luck. It wasn't.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Six months earlier, Admiral Yamamoto had a problem. Pearl Harbor had sunk battleships,

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,000
but the American carriers were not in port that morning.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,500
So he drew a trap on the map: attack Midway, and the American carriers would have to come out.

8
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,500
But in Hawaii, in a basement with no windows, Commander Joseph Rochefort was reading his mail.

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:44,000
His team had broken enough of the Japanese naval code to know one thing: the target was called AF.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
So they sent a fake message: Midway is short of water.

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Two days later, Tokyo reported that AF was short of water. The trap had been reversed.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Japan had four carriers. America had three. On paper, it should not have been close.
